WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.130
- The CDC is now recommending
the Pfizer vaccine

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.180
for children ages five to 11.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.060
What does that mean?

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.000
What are the benefits?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.960
What are the drawbacks?

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.530
And how you can help in the
battle against misinformation

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.690
with our good friend, the Surgeon
General, Dr. Vivek Murthy.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.730
let's get started, peewoop.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:15.940
We have a lot to talk about.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.740
- Yes, a lot's happened
since you and I last chatted.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.450
- Yeah, now we have the vaccine

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.730
that is more widely available for kids,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.710
and that's a topic I
really wanna dive into.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.400
But first, let's talk about
this misinformation toolkit

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.750
that you've published.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.610
Tell me more about that.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.400
- And we did that, not 'cause
how misinformation is new,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.040
but because in the last few years,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.560
we've seen a dramatic increase

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.841
in the scale and the
speed and sophistication

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:40.090
with which this
misinformation is spreading.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.580
So, we wanted to call attention to that

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.170
and let everyone know
that there were steps

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.007
all of us could and needed to take.

00:00:45.007 --> 00:00:46.290
And here's why this is so important

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.420
because there's a recent
poll that just came out

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.340
that showed that close to 80% of people

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.170
either believe or think
some of the myths out there

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.280
about COVID-19 are actually true.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.740
- What I love about the approach

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.460
that's really highlighted in this toolkit

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.480
is that you wanna lead with
an empathetic approach.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.830
You wanna be not so much challenging

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.410
what people currently believe,

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.130
but sort of coming from
a place of understanding

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.570
of where they're hearing
it, why they're worried.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.840
- One of the things that we
advocate for in this toolkit

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.240
is first, just taking
a pause to understand

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.450
what people's motivations are,

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.760
what their concerns are,
what's important to them.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.810
If we don't take an empathetic approach,

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.410
if we don't give people
the benefit of the doubt

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.840
before we judge or shame
them, then we lose them.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.400
We don't have the
opportunity to support folks

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.070
in reaching that shared goal.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.600
I haven't heard of a single person's mind

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.380
who's been changed by
being shamed or blamed.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.430
So, the bottom line is
those approaches don't work.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.606
- Yeah, tell me what
vaccine has been authorized

00:01:40.606 --> 00:01:42.620
by the FDA, under the EUA,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.180
and what are the steps
that parents should take

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.620
to getting this vaccine for their kids.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:47.453
- Well, I'm glad we're talking about this

00:01:47.453 --> 00:01:49.850
'cause this is a landmark moment

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.220
not just for parents like me
who have kids five through 11,

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.080
but for all of us

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.920
who wanna see this
pandemic come to an end.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.734
With the recent FDA authorization

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:59.470
and the CDC recommendation of the vaccine

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.303
for kids five through 11,

00:02:00.303 --> 00:02:01.950
and this is the Pfizer vaccine, mind you,

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.380
we now have 28 million children,
28 million more people,

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.070
who have come under the umbrella

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.470
potentially of being vaccinated.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.110
But here's what parents
really need to know.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.000
Number one,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.490
the vaccine was rigorously
tested in clinical trials

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.490
and it was put through
the same review process

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.360
by the FDA and CDC that we
put any other vaccine through.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.070
And what they found in that review process

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.170
was that this vaccine
was highly effective,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.880
more than 90% effective,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.170
at protecting our kids
from symptomatic COVID.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.001
The second thing they found
is that the safety profile

00:02:30.001 --> 00:02:32.430
of the vaccine was actually
really, really good.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.050
And when children did have side effects,

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.250
they were a sore arm, fatigue,

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.110
a headache, occasionally a fever,

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.480
but those symptoms went
away within a day or two,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.750
and what the children were left with

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.290
was longer-term protection.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.123
And very importantly,

00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:47.670
they did not see any
serious adverse effects.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.570
- Do you view this authorization
for five to 11 year old

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.200
as a potential off-ramp

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.850
for some of the residual mask
mandates that still exist,

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.290
whether it's in schools, in hospitals?

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.810
- Okay, well, so I think the
more people get vaccinated,

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.085
the more we have a chance of getting cases

00:03:01.085 --> 00:03:03.010
to come down and stay down,

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.450
and then that's really gonna be our key

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.370
to an off-ramp with things like masks

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.690
and other restrictions as well.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.070
Kids, in addition to getting COVID-19,

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.870
also can spread COVID-19.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.540
There was a notion out there before

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.070
that kids don't transmit the virus.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.570
We absolutely found that is not the case.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.140
They do transmit the virus,
they contribute to spread.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.253
And so, yes, getting 28 million
more children vaccinated

00:03:22.253 --> 00:03:24.380
will absolutely help reduce the spread,

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.170
help get cases down, keep 'em down.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.330
And that's when we can start to get rid of

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.650
some of the restrictions that
we currently have right now.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.950
- How does getting your child
vaccinated protect grandma?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:34.870
- Oh, great question.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.940
We know, again, that children
can transmit the virus,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.210
that has definitely been proven.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.352
We also know that when
children then see folks

00:03:41.352 --> 00:03:44.093
who are vulnerable like
grandparents, for example,

00:03:44.093 --> 00:03:45.716
especially those who
have not been vaccinated,

00:03:45.716 --> 00:03:48.260
there's a real risk they can
pass on the virus to them.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.093
And that's important

00:03:49.093 --> 00:03:50.880
because we've seen the
vast majority of deaths

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.650
that have taken place from COVID-19

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.430
has occurred among the elderly
population, those above 65.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.010
And finally, Mike, I think it's important

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.500
that we recognize one thing
that COVID has taught us, right,

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.690
is that our health really does depend

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:03.523
on what other people do, right?

00:04:03.523 --> 00:04:04.356
- Yeah.

00:04:04.356 --> 00:04:07.060
- And what we've learned from
other viruses and illnesses

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.290
in the past is the more
of us get vaccinated,

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.150
the more of a wall we build
around those who are vulnerable.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.870
- Yeah, and a very specific question

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.030
that I see come up quite
often on social media

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.310
and from my patients is on
the topic of myocarditis,

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:20.610
the inflammation of the heart.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.480
We didn't even see that
in the Pfizer study

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:24.830
for five to 11 year olds.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:28.910
Do you think the study had
sufficient participants

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.350
to rule that out?

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.270
And if it does happen, what does it mean?

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.010
How does it compare to getting myocarditis

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.770
from actual COVID-19?

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.870
- The trial that was done
for kids five through 11

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.490
had several thousand
children in it, right?

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.780
So, they were able to detect side effects

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.620
that would happen with
any reasonable frequency.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.910
And thankfully, they didn't see
any serious adverse effects.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.490
Now, is there a chance that there could be

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.190
a very rare side effect that crops up?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.130
There's always that chance,

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.760
but everything we do is
a risk-benefit, right?

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.120
And what we have to compare
the risk of any vaccine to

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.880
is to the risk of getting COVID itself.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.430
And there, what we do know
is that people who get COVID

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.560
do have a significantly higher risk

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.090
of actually having cardiac
involvement like myocarditis.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.260
We also know that they
have a risk of blood clots,

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.660
they have a risk of on COVID,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.790
and a whole host of other issues,

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.860
which you don't see with vaccines.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:20.150
- I think the reality of
how prevalent COVID is now

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:23.710
in our society that
you're basically choosing

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.800
between getting the vaccine and
getting COVID at this point.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.590
Because I don't think
there's a child out there

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.740
who you can say they probably
won't experience COVID.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.080
I think that it's so prevalent

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.910
that you're almost having
to make the choice,

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.690
it's between the vaccine or COVID.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.760
And in that case, if you
look at the myocarditis

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.330
that has happened in the slightly
higher age range for kids,

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.520
it's been so few in comparison

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.800
to getting myocarditis from COVID-19,

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.310
you're essentially making the decision

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.750
between one of two paths.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.550
And we wanna make the
path of least disease,

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:58.160
least infection, least complications.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.560
And COVID-19 has a lot of
complications, as you said.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.130
So, really, that's the
take-home point for parents.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:06.260
How do you see this
misinformation playing out

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.840
with the topic of
infertility for children?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.210
Because that's something a lot
of parents are worried about

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.000
because their children five to 11

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.920
don't have that issue at
that point, obviously,

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.170
but then, later in life,

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.650
is that something you're concerned about,

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.320
even perhaps for your own children?

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.390
- Yeah, I'm glad you raised it

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.910
because there are about
1/3 of folks out there

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.750
who either believe or are unsure

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.730
about this myth around infertility.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.740
The truth is that there is
nothing in the data that we have,

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.270
in the science, that lends
any credence to that rumor.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:37.500
There is no link between
the vaccine and infertility.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.680
And that's actually why I'm getting

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.640
my five-year-old vaccinated, too.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.080
Because, of course, I want
him to have a healthy future.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.190
I want him to be healthy in all ways.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.810
I would love for him to
have a family one day,

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.598
if he wants to, but I'm not concerned

00:06:48.598 --> 00:06:50.680
that the vaccine is gonna
inhibit any of that.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.970
If anything, I feel the vaccine
will give him a greater shot

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.270
of leading a healthier life

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.380
and not having complications from COVID,

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.940
and that's what we all want as parents.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.470
- What's your guidance on
receiving the COVID-19 vaccine

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.036
for your five to 11 year old

00:07:03.036 --> 00:07:05.170
and getting other
vaccines at the same time?

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:08.890
- The good news is you can
get other vaccines as well.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:11.410
It's very important to
get vaccinated for flu,

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.110
you just need to get
it at a different site.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.640
So, we have two arms, so we
can get a shot in each arm.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.237
- (laughs) What would you tell parents

00:07:16.237 --> 00:07:18.686
who have an 11 year old who's
close to her 12th birthday?

00:07:18.686 --> 00:07:21.320
Should they wait for
the 30 microgram dose?

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.220
- Yes, I would say don't wait.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.670
I'd say go ahead and get your dose now

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.330
and if your child is 11,
they'll get 10 micrograms.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.320
If they're 12 by the time they're
due for their second dose,

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:34.120
then they'll get 30
micrograms at that point.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.340
But the reason not to wait

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.510
is that you don't wanna delay your child

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.250
starting to build protection.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.650
And they will start to build protection

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.320
with that 10 microgram dose.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.640
Especially with as much
COVID as we have circulating,

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.340
the faster kids get protected, the better.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.278
- Are there any children
that you would recommend

00:07:48.278 --> 00:07:51.390
to not get vaccinated or hold
off waiting to get vaccinated?

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:52.476
- So, I would say the only reason

00:07:52.476 --> 00:07:54.870
to hold off getting vaccinated

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.230
is if you have a specific allergy

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.410
to a component of the Pfizer vaccine.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.820
That's very rare, people
generally don't have that.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:05.357
But if you have an allergy
to foods or to eggs,

00:08:05.357 --> 00:08:06.610
for example, or other things,

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.210
you don't need to avoid
getting vaccinated.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.530
We want people to go
ahead and get vaccinated.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:12.900
- Yeah, I think a lot of patients

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.440
and parents have questions.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.820
If their child has a unique condition,

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:21.770
whether it's a platelet
condition, some other allergy,

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.920
perhaps a heart condition or
diabetes runs in the family,

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.690
and they get worried if their
child is at a higher risk

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.630
to having side effects,
is any of that true?

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:33.080
- Well, so generally, we
haven't seen any concerns

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:34.990
with children with
other medical conditions

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:35.910
getting the vaccine.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:36.743
That's good news.

00:08:36.743 --> 00:08:38.300
In fact, I would say the flip is true,

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.120
which is if you have
other medical conditions,

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.010
then we know from our
experience with COVID,

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:45.560
that increases the risk
of you having bad outcomes

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.260
if you get COVID-19.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.558
So, in my mind, it's actually
all the more important

00:08:49.558 --> 00:08:51.810
for children with other medical conditions

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.480
to get vaccinated to protect them against

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:55.710
the bad outcomes of the virus.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.165
One of the things that's
really important, I think,

00:08:57.165 --> 00:09:00.340
is for us to recognize that
getting our kids vaccinated

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:01.564
is also about helping to address

00:09:01.564 --> 00:09:03.840
the profound mental health toll

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.410
that our kids have sustained
over the last 20 months.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:09.410
Rates of anxiety and
depression and loneliness

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.480
rise among any groups of children.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.040
And this is so sad to see
and it's heartbreaking,

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.410
but we can do something about it.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.850
That's where the vaccine is so helpful.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.260
- It's a very holistic approach

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:19.910
and a as a family medicine doctor

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.330
who's also an osteopathic
physician by training,

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.680
I very much appreciate you
thinking in those terms.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.300
- And I'm really hopeful,
also, at this moment.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.717
And I know that sometimes
you read the news

00:09:28.717 --> 00:09:31.450
and it can feel like it's
doom and gloom all the time,

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.880
but there are so many reasons

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.130
at this particular point
in time to be hopeful.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.770
We have not just one, but
three vaccines available.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.990
We have 190 million plus people

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.220
who have been fully vaccinated.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.490
We have our kids back in school.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.130
We have vaccines for kids five through 11,

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.380
and we're finding ways to
get back to our way of life,

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.310
but we can only do it together.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.680
And that's why it's not just about doctors

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.740
like me and you having conversations,

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.220
it's about people recognizing
the power they have

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:56.280
because of their voice,

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.110
because of their trusted relationships.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.160
They can be the person
who makes a difference

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.440
in someone else's
decision to get protected

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:03.460
by getting vaccinated.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.970
- Dr. Murthy, thank you
so much for educating us,

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.769
empowering us to help my
viewers and myself and my family

00:10:08.769 --> 00:10:10.780
to make the right
decisions about our health.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.160
And I hope we continue meeting
up with this misinformation.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:16.670
We have a toolkit now that
I can arm my residents with,

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.470
community leaders with, and
we continue to thank you

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.510
for the work that you've been doing.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.343
So, thank you for that.

00:10:21.343 --> 00:10:22.950
- I so appreciate that, Mike.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.500
- I had a difficult patient encounter,

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.730
click here to check that out.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.808
And as always, stay happy and healthy.

00:10:27.808 --> 00:10:30.808
